Host-compiler fixes for llvm/clang svn r148911 (January 2012) built with a
current Apple clang and libc++. None of them change what the built clang
generates:
- llvm-build is Python 2; converted with lib2to3 (python3.12 -m lib2to3).
- 'template' keyword for dependent template names (IntervalMap, PointerUnion,
  ExprConstant), and a never-instantiated ASTVector member typo.
- CFG.h iterators declare pointer/reference types as LLVM 3.3 does; libc++
  checks them when building vectors from succ_begin/pred_begin.
- "%"PRIu64 literal in VTableBuilder.cpp parses as a C++11 UDL.
build-clang.sh also builds this revision with -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks
-fno-strict-aliasing -fwrapv: without them the optimizer of a clang built by
a current host compiler crashes (jump threading) on the CEF wrapper.

